8. TERMINATION AND REINSTATEMENT
======================================================================

Any material breach of this License automatically terminates the rights
granted to the breaching party under this License.

The Licensor may, but is not obligated to, provide written notice
describing an alleged breach.

Except for intentional unauthorized Commercial Use, unauthorized
resale, sublicensing, transfer, Product Distribution, patent litigation
described in Section 7, or a repeated material breach, rights terminated
for a curable breach are automatically reinstated if the breach is fully
cured within thirty (30) calendar days after the Licensor provides
written notice.

Intentional unauthorized Commercial Use, unauthorized resale,
sublicensing, transfer, Product Distribution, patent-litigation
termination, or repeated material breach may be reinstated only by the
Licensor's express written consent.

Reinstatement does not waive claims, remedies, fees, damages, or other
rights arising from conduct that occurred while this License was
violated or terminated.

Upon termination, the breaching party must immediately cease all use,
modification, distribution, access, commercialization, and other conduct
that depends on rights granted by this License.

